# f1 = sumOrNone. In `total += d[i].x` the read by name asks its site in line and is asked for a number, because the sum is its only user. Under `?? 0` and `|| 7` the field reaches the
# sum over a join beside a written number: it is reckoned with as a number there too. A record without the field, a null, a text leave the typed copy of the loop, which runs on as written.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = GetValueAtSiteOrAbsent {{*}} key="x"
# RUN(SEVEN): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# SEVEN: = GetValueAtSiteOrAbsent {{*}} key="x"
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWER: sumOrNone 2.5 2.2591.5 4.5
# ANSWER-NEXT: sumOrSeven 2.5 23.2591.5 4.5
# ANSWER-NEXT: exited with 0
